    "superseded": [
      {
        "extensionId": "66163",
        "instructionSender": "0x6D49c54D2F75214616a0964Bd52c695384f1b6E2",
        "retiredAt": "2026-08-11T23:11:16Z",
        "reason": "Its authorizeRedemption took the decision input alone and relayed it unmodified, which a security review correctly called an unauthenticated signing-decision relay: any caller could name an obligation that did not exist. Superseded by a sender that checks the obligation against SignetRegistry. It never carried a live TEE machine, so no instruction was ever executed through it."
      },
      {
        "extensionId": "66164",
        "instructionSender": "0xDd8aA7A4f43f01258A426a30d02032821De9bc6e",
        "retiredAt": "2026-08-14T06:51:34Z",
        "reason": "It checked the obligation against SignetRegistry, which is why it superseded 66163, but its authorizeRedemption still accepted a caller-authored message: the caller chose destination, amount, reference, tag and window, and the contract checked those for internal consistency rather than truth. Superseded by gate B, whose authorizeRedemption(uint256,uint32) takes a request id and a generation and resolves every payment field from FAssets itself, so no parameter exists through which a caller could express one. It never carried a live TEE machine, so no instruction was ever executed through it."
      },
      {
        "extensionId": "66244",
        "instructionSender": "0x3FFA63a3bf21a626c1B391D2577b1800e67F5Be0",
        "retiredAt": "2026-08-14T08:15:23Z",
        "reason": "Its authorizeRedemption gated on action.state != NONE, so an action already moved to AUTHORIZED, REFUSED or EVIDENCE_FINALIZED could be instructed again, and it kept no record of having dispatched, so repeated calls while the action was still REQUESTED each produced a fresh instruction. A 256-run fuzz over caller sequences found ten dispatches for one obligation. Superseded by a sender that admits only REQUESTED and records the dispatch on chain before the external call, giving at most one instruction per (requestId, generation). It never carried a live TEE machine, so no instruction was ever executed through it."
      }
    ],
